nt/tech-design.md:37:| Process-scoped shadowing needs exact read rule | Tech Design Question 7 | Design defines an active-source resolver that combines project-scoped and process-scoped attachments, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, and excludes detached rows. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:51:| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:54:| 6 | How should shell/process surfaces stay coherent across project and process scope? | Keep project shell source summaries for project-wide management. Process work surfaces show current sources after active-source resolution, including process-scoped shadowing and applicable project-scoped rows. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:70:attached, understand whether it can receive writes, refresh stale or missing\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:76:sandboxed filesystem is only a disposable working copy. Fastify is the source\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:78:process access, resolves shadowing rules, coordinates refresh, and records\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:147:| Environment refresh seam | Refresh/recovery paths | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated source refresh seam over existing process/environment services rather than assuming a full source-management implementation already exists |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:158:| Process-scoped attach updates current process source refs immediately | The epic says a process-scoped attachment belongs to one process as current source state and becomes visible immediately | `attachProcessSource` persists the source row and adds its id to that process's current source refs in the same orchestration path |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:159:| Process scope shadows project scope only in current-source reads | Same repo can be useful both project-wide and process-specific | Durable rows can coexist; resolver picks process-scoped row for that process when identity/ref collide |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:182:└── source-management.ts                         # NEW: Fastify routes for attach/update/refresh/detach/provenance\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:188:├── source-refresh.service.ts                    # NEW: refresh request handling and pending/settled result shaping\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:224:| `MaterialsSectionReader` | Modified | Resolve current process sources with process-scoped shadowing and detached filtering | PlatformStore | AC-2.1, AC-3.1, AC-6.1 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:251:  refreshStatus: v.union(v.literal('idle'), v.literal('pending'), v.literal('failed')),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:252:  refreshRequestedAt: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:280:- `lastHydratedResolvedRef`: the commit SHA or resolved ref hydrated 